## Why This Is Asked
Tests for streaming pipelines must cover correctness under huge load, fault tolerance, and operational safety. This question probes end-to-end strategy, data quality, drift, and rollback semantics, not isolated unit tests.

## Key Concepts
- End-to-end streaming test harness
- Exactly-once vs at-least-once semantics
- Latency budgets and tail latency
- Backpressure and circuit breakers
- Data quality and drift detection
- Rollback and reconciliation
- Replayable synthetic data generation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-test snippet showing a Kafka consumer with sequence checks
const consumer = new KafkaConsumer({ groupId: 'tester' });
let lastSeq = 0;
consumer.on('message', (msg) => {
  if (msg.seq <= lastSeq) throw new Error('out-of-order');
  lastSeq = msg.seq;
  // validate idempotent write
  writeIfNotExists(msg.key, msg.value);
});
```

